# Reading Russian news: headlines, participles, verbal nouns
subtitle: "Read a short Russian news item: headlines without a verb, откры́тие and строи́тельство, шеф, рабо́тающий в Петербу́рге, as Masha reads Tom the news about his win."
tags: ["russian","russian news","russian reading","participles","verbal nouns"]
teaches: ["reading/reading-news","grammar/participles","grammar/passive"]
thumb: "band \"Read Russian news headlines\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"For and against in Russian: против, ради, среди","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/187-russian-for-and-against.cast"}

## Reading Russian news: headlines, participles, verbal nouns
